  "query_preview": "..Not a cloud in the sky over Utah and southwest\nWyoming this morning with strong high pressure centered near the\nFour Corners. It'll be another dry and mild day with maxes\naveraging 10F above seasonal normals. Though the ridge weakens and\nshifts east tomorrow, dry conditions will continue with\ntemperatures similar to today.\n\nThe weakening of the ridge will allow for a weak storm system to\nmove across the area Tuesday, moving in during the early morning\nand persisting through the afternoon. Impacts will be minimal,\nwith temperatures expected to drop a couple of degrees for Tuesday\nafternoon with a few showers developing over the higher terrain\nduring the afternoon. After that, dry conditions look to persist\nthrough the remainder of the work week with temperatures staying\nmild.\n\nBy late next weekend, the majority of guidance is showing at least\nsome impacts from a strong Pacific Northwest storm system.\nHowever, there is considerable spread with regard to the timing,\ntrack, and strength of this system. Still, with little else of\ninterest on the horizon, will be keeping a close eye on the\npotential solutions over the next several days.",
